From 904f330e4411dd9feb77b2cd4d622f0f5db1b458 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:12:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 106/109] fix(executorch, onnxruntime): the load probe fails
 closed, and say exactly what to install

Review round 3 of B204.

The image-route probe let the load go ahead on anything but an empty 404:
a timeout, a transport error, a 5xx, a crash or a watchdog reset during
the probe all counted as "route present". Now only the engine's 4xx
refusal of an image request without an image (other than 404) lets the
load continue. Any 404, whatever its body, means no route. Anything else
refuses the load (NonRetryable) with what happened, for example "it did
not answer (Network error: CURL error: Timeout was reached)" or "it
answered HTTP 500 (...)", and a cancelled load is reported as cancelled.
The empty-body rule now applies only to the request-time 502 fallback,
where a bodied 404 passes through.

The remedies now say what works. backend_utils.cpp
find_external_backend_binary sends a *_bin value that does not look like
a path to the install flow, and the onnxruntime install repository is
lemonade-sdk/ort-server, which has no image route. So for ort the text is
"set onnxruntime.cpu_bin to the absolute path of an ort-server that serves
/classify/image (for example ianbmacdonald/ort-server v0.2.0-musl or
later), since a version tag there installs lemonade-sdk/ort-server". For
et it is "put an et-server v0.2.0 or later on PATH; lemonade does not
download et-server". The text no longer names the 0.4.0 default.

The fake engine gains FAKE_PROBE_HANG, FAKE_PROBE_500, FAKE_PROBE_404_BODY
and FAKE_PROBE_CRASH, which misbehave only on an image request without an
image. test_519a-d check that each one refuses the et and ort load with
its outcome, and test_517 now pins the exact status and envelope: tflite's
engine 404 passes through as a 404 invalid_request_error, and et/ort loads
are refused with 500 model_load_error.

